{"name":"Broomstick","hex":"#74462d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"broomstick","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The handle of a broom (sweeping tool); (sometimes) the entire broom.","A broom imbued with magic, enabling one to fly astride the handle."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fly on a broomstick, as witches are said to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broomstick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Broomstick (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Broomstick (1901–1931) was a Thoroughbred race horse whose most important win was in the 1904 Travers Stakes. Broomstick then became one of the great sires in American racing history, leading the North American sire list in 1913, 1914 and 1915. He was inducted into the National Museum of Racing and Hall of Fame in 1956."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/George_Odom_and_Broomstick.jpg/330px-George_Odom_and_Broomstick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broomstick_(horse)","wikidata":"Q4975349"},{"title":"Broom","blocks":[{"text":"A broom, also known as a broomstick, is a cleaning tool, consisting of usually stiff fibers attached to, and roughly parallel to, a cylindrical handle, the broomstick. It is thus a variety of brush with a long handle. It is commonly used in combination with a dustpan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/BroomsforSale.jpg/330px-BroomsforSale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broom","wikidata":"Q172833"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Broom_Han_Dynasty_British_Museum_MAS.776.jpg/500px-Broom_Han_Dynasty_British_Museum_MAS.776.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Broom_Han_Dynasty_British_Museum_MAS.77